===[ The first AI Era (1950s - 1970s) ]===
- Researchers believed intelligence could be programmed directly
- Their idea was simple:
  """
    Human Intelligence
          |
      'Write Rules'
          |
    Computer becomes intelligent
  """
- Suppose we want to 'recognize a cat', A 'programmer write a rules':
  """
    If has wiskers
       & has tail
       & has four legs
       & meows
    then
      cat
  """
  ->> This approach is called > 'Rule-based AI' or 'Symbolic Ai'
      The 'computer never learns', it only 'follows rules/instructions'
      (This is what is called 'programming intelligence')

  # QUESTION:[ What this approach 'Rule-based AI' fails? ]=====================
  # - Real life is messy. consider cats:
  #   . Some cats have no tails
  #   . Some cats do not meow 
  #   . Some are sleeping
  #   . Some are enormous
  #   ...
  # - Soon You end up writing 'thousands of rules':
  #   IF
  #     ...
  #   ELSE IF
  #     ...
  #   ELSE IF
  #     ...
  #   ELSE
  #   -> Eventually: 'IMPOSSIBLE'
  # - The world contains too many exceptions, Researchers realized something 
  #   profound

===[ Birth Of Machine Learning ]===
* Researchers realized something profound:
  - 'Instead of teaching computers':
    """ Rules """ maybe 

  - 'We should teach them'
    """ Examples """
  ->> 'This idea changed AI Forver' <<-

  - Instead of this: (Rule-based AI: programming intelligence)
    """
      programmer
          |
      Write Rules
          |
      Computer
    """
  - We now have:
    """
             Data
              |
      Learning algorithm
              |
            Model
    """
  - We program
    """ The ability to learn (algorithm)""" instead of """ Rules """ This is
    what is called 'Machine learning'.

  - Example: 
    * Imagine 'recognizing handwritten digits'
      - Traditional Programming:
        """
          programmer
              |
          find every possible shpae of (7) all cases (explicitly)
              |
          Impossible
        """
      - Machine Learning:
        """
          thousands of images
                  |
          Learning algorithm
                  |
          Model discovers the pattern (implicitly)
        """
    ->> The 'programmer no longer writes' the 'rules', the algorithm 'discovers'
        'them automatically'
    -->> "This is a huge conceptual shift" <<--

===[ Machine Learning Definition ]===
* Arthur samuel (1959) gave one of the 'earliest definitions':
  """
    A 'computer learns' from 'experience' if its 'performance' at a 'task' 
    'improves' with experience.
  """
  - year later, Tom mitchell formalized it:
  """
    A computer program is said to learn from experience 'E' with respect to 
    some task 'T' and performance measure 'P', if its performance at 'T' as
    measured by 'P' improves with 'E'.
  """
  -->> Notice Something: There is no 'mention' of 'neural networks', Machine
       Learning is much broader.

